e('On x86-64, translating one address means walking four tables, so every load or store would need four extra memory reads. Memory would be five times slower.','An uncached four-level x86-64 walk to a 4 KiB page reads four entries before the data access. That simplified read count is not a universal 5× latency prediction.','Cachesoverlap/modesmatter.')
