f(7,'workedExample','Without PCIDs, an ordinary CR3 write invalidates non-global entries. Enabled global mappings may survive. PCID tags can preserve translations across suitable no-flush switches, but invalidation is still required for changed mappings or reused tags. Shared-mm task switches need no flush solely because a different thread runs. With KPTI, global translations are restricted to mappings safe in both views.','Global/noflushprecise.',pt)
